            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> is util here going to be available after this change?\r\n\r\nYes, it should be. `util`'s value is resolved when closure runs, not when it is captured.\r\n\r\n> if lsp_complete_configured_servers isn't used on some version of Nvim that also doesn't need util, then why did we define lsp_complete_configured_servers at all?\r\n\r\nTo be honest, I wanted to get rid of an extra file read, but you're right. `lsp_complete_configured_servers` and some other definitions can be moved lower to save more milliseconds on the newer Neovim versions. Should I move those too, or did I misunderstand you and you're suggesting reverting for clarity?",
            "commit_id": "45891046c8493c56deee9d9ce3a04baf28deba80",
